SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssttrrffttiimmee() function conforms to ISO/IEC 9899:1990 (“ISO C90”) with a
     lot of extensions including ‘%C’, ‘%D’, ‘%E*’, ‘%e’, ‘%G’, ‘%g’, ‘%h’,
     ‘%k’, ‘%l’, ‘%n’, ‘%O*’, ‘%R’, ‘%r’, ‘%s’, ‘%T’, ‘%t’, ‘%u’, ‘%V’, ‘%z’,
     ‘%+’.

     The peculiar week number and year in the replacements of ‘%G’, ‘%g’ and
     ‘%V’ are defined in ISO 8601.  The ssttrrffttiimmee__ll() function conforms to IEEE
     Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

BBUUGGSS
     There is no conversion specification for the phase of the moon.

     The ssttrrffttiimmee() function does not correctly handle multibyte characters in
     the _f_o_r_m_a_t argument.

